(1422, 'Carding machine', 47, 81, 265, 471, 352, 3, 'Toyoda / Japan', 'TM-8SL', '1989', '', '<p>Carding machine is a crucial piece of equipment used in the textile industry to disentangle, clean, and intermix fibers, such as cotton or wool, to produce a continuous web or sliver suitable for further processing. The process involves passing the fibers through a series of wire-covered rollers that comb and align the fibers, removing impurities and short fibers to create a uniform, continuous strand. Carding helps improve the quality and consistency of the yarn, making it an essential step in the yarn manufacturing process</p>\r\n', '', '', '', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '', 0, 0, 0, '', '', 1, '', '', 1, 'J A Chinthaka', 'chinthaka@uom.lk', '0112650301', '', '                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  ', NULL, 'CARDING_MACHINE.jpg', '', '', '', 0, 509, '2024-09-02 13:06:54', 509, '2024-09-02 16:30:55', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1423, 'Draw Frame', 47, 81, 265, 471, 352, 3, 'Hara Shokki Seisakusho Ltd/ Japan', 'DX-500', '1989', '', '<p>Draw frame is a machine used in the textile manufacturing process to further improve the quality of slivers produced by the carding or combing processes. The primary function of the draw frame is to blend and straighten the fibers while simultaneously reducing the sliver thickness and increasing its uniformity through drafting. It achieves this by drawing the sliver through a series of pairs of rollers that rotate at progressively faster speeds, aligning the fibers parallel to each other. This process enhances the evenness and strength of the sliver, which is critical for producing high-quality yarn in the subsequent spinning processes. The draw frame is essential in ensuring consistent quality in yarn production by correcting irregularities and optimizing fiber alignment</p>\r\n', '', '', '', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '', 0, 0, 0, '', '', 1, '', '', 1, 'J A Chinthaka', 'chinthaka@uom.lk', '0112650301', '', '                                                                                                                                                                     ', NULL, 'DRAW_FRAM.jpg', '', '', '', 0, 509, '2024-09-02 14:43:21', 509, '2024-09-02 16:30:43', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1424, 'Speed Frame', 47, 81, 265, 471, 352, 3, 'Sanyu Boki Co Ltd, /Japan', '', '1989', '', '<p>Speed frame, also known as a roving frame or simplex machine, is an essential machine in the textile spinning process that converts slivers from the draw frame into roving. Roving is a slightly twisted, finer strand that serves as an intermediate product before the final spinning stage. The speed frame performs three key functions: drafting, twisting, and winding.The speed frame plays a critical role in preparing fibers for spinning by ensuring consistent thickness, proper fiber alignment, and sufficient twist, which are crucial for producing high-quality yarn</p>\r\n', '', '', '', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '', 0, 0, 0, '', '', 1, '', '', 1, 'J A Chinthaka', 'chinthaka@uom.lk', '0112650301', '', '                                                                                                                                                                     ', NULL, 'SPEED_FRAME.jpg', '', '', '', 0, 509, '2024-09-02 14:56:19', 509, '2024-09-02 16:30:19', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1425, 'Ring Frame', 47, 81, 265, 471, 352, 3, 'Susuki/Japan', '', '1989', '', '<p>Ring frame is a type of spinning machine used in the textile industry to produce yarn from roving through a process called ring spinning. It is one of the most widely used and traditional methods of spinning due to its ability to produce high-quality yarns with excellent strength, uniformity, and fineness. The ring frame performs three main functions: drafting, twisting, and winding.The ring frame consists of a ring, traveler, spindle, and bobbin system, where the spindle rotates at high speed, and the traveler moves along the ring, inserting the twist into the yarn. Ring spinning is known for producing yarns that are strong, smooth, and ideal for a wide range of textile applications, from fine fabrics to industrial materials.</p>\r\n', '', '', '', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '', 0, 0, 0, '', '', 1, '', '', 1, 'J A Chinthaka', 'chinthaka@uom.lk', '0112650301', '', '                                                                                                                                                                     ', NULL, 'RING_FRAME.jpg', '', '', '', 0, 509, '2024-09-02 15:08:00', 509, '2024-09-02 16:29:59', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1426, 'Speed cone winder/ Splicer winder', 47, 81, 265, 471, 352, 3, 'Murata / Japan', '', '1989', '', '<p>splicer winder is a specialized type of winding machine used in the textile industry to wind yarn onto packages such as cones or spools while also incorporating a splicing function. The splicing mechanism automatically joins yarn ends when a break occurs or when changing bobbins, creating a nearly seamless, knot-free connection. This results in a continuous length of yarn without the bulky knots that can cause issues in further processing like weaving or knitting.Splicer winders are widely used in the production of high-quality yarns where smoothness and continuity are essential, such as in fine fabrics, high-speed knitting, or critical industrial applications</p>\r\n', '', '', '', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '', 0, 0, 0, '', '', 1, '', '', 1, 'J A Chinthaka', 'chinthaka@uom.lk', '0112650301', '', '                                                                                                                                                                     ', NULL, 'SPLICER_WINDER.jpg', '', '', '', 0, 509, '2024-09-02 15:17:09', 509, '2024-09-02 16:29:34', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1427, 'Doubler winder', 47, 81, 265, 471, 352, 3, 'Murata / Japan', '', '1989', '', '<p>Doubler winder, also known as a doubling winder, is a type of winding machine used in the textile industry to combine two or more yarns together into a single, unified package. This process, known as doubling, is essential for creating thicker, stronger, or more complex yarns by winding multiple strands together with precise control over tension and alignment.Doubler winders are commonly used in producing yarns for heavier fabrics, technical textiles, or specialty applications where combined yarn properties are needed, offering a reliable and efficient way to achieve the desired yarn characteristics.</p>\r\n', '', '', '', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '', 0, 0, 0, '', '', 1, '', '', 1, 'J A Chinthaka', 'chinthaka@uom.lk', '0112650301', '', '                                                                                                                                                                     ', NULL, 'HIGH_SPEED_DOUBLER_WINDER_.jpg', '', '', '', 0, 509, '2024-09-02 15:31:26', 509, '2024-09-02 16:29:17', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1428, 'Two for one twister', 47, 81, 265, 471, 352, 3, 'Murata / Japan', '', '1989', '', '<p>Two-for-One (TFO) twister is a specialized machine used in the textile industry for twisting yarns, commonly employed in the production of plied yarns. The TFO twister is highly efficient because it inserts two twists into the yarn for every rotation of the spindle, effectively doubling the twisting speed and productivity compared to traditional twisting machines.The Two-for-One twister is widely used in producing yarns for knitting, weaving, and technical textiles, offering improved efficiency, reduced operational costs, and superior yarn quality.</p>\r\n', '', '', '', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '', 0, 0, 0, '', '', 1, '', '', 1, 'J A Chinthaka', 'chinthaka@uom.lk', '0112650301', '', '                                                                                                                                                                     ', NULL, 'TWO_FOR_ONE_TWISTER.jpg', '', '', '', 0, 509, '2024-09-02 15:36:14', 509, '2024-09-02 15:51:11', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1429, 'Air jet texturing machine', 47, 81, 265, 471, 352, 1, 'SSM/ Switzerland', 'DP5-TF/TC', '2016', '', '<p>Air jet texturing machine is a textile machine used to create textured yarns from synthetic fibers such as polyester, nylon, or polypropylene. The process, known as air jet texturing, uses high-pressure air jets to create loops, crimps, and bulk in the filaments, transforming flat continuous filament yarns into yarns that resemble spun or natural fibers in appearance and feel.Air jet texturing provides a cost-effective and environmentally friendly method for producing high-performance yarns with a natural look and feel, enhancing the aesthetic and functional properties of synthetic yarns in various textile products</p>\r\n', '', NULL, '', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '', 0, 0, 0, '', '', 1, '', '', 1, 'J A Chinthaka', 'chinthaka@uom.lk', '0112650301', '', '                                                                                    ', NULL, 'AIR_JET_TEXTURING_.jpg', NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 509, '2024-09-02 15:47:31', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1430, 'Torrefaction Reactor', 47, 81, 256, 386, 315, 1, '', '', '0000', 'isharaw@uom.lk', '<p>The lab-scale cylindrical torrefaction reactor available in the Department of Chemical and<br />\r\nProcess Engineering, University of Moratuwa can be used for lab-scale experiments and it<br />\r\nconsists of a cylindrical heating coil with a Stainless-Steel reactor, temperature controller, and<br />\r\ninert gas feeding system. The weight loss of products will be recorded by varying the<br />\r\ntorrefaction temperature and residence time. The condensable fraction of the volatiles will be<br />\r\nrecovered, and analyzed for the possibility of dilute acid washing of biomass.</p>\r\n', '', NULL, '', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '', 0, 0, 0, '', '', 1, 'PG students Reasearch', '', 1, 'Ishara', 'isharaw@uom.lk', 'EXT 4100', '', '                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            ', NULL, 'IMG-20240829-WA00112.jpg', NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 485, '2024-09-04 11:52:12', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1431, 'Ultra-High-Performance Liquid Chromatography', 11, 0, 78, 109, 365, 1, 'Agilent Technologies', '1290 * 1260', '0000', '', '', '', '', '', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '', 0, 0, 0, '', '', 0, 'Ministry of Development Strategies and International Trade', '', 1, 'Nishanthi Ratnayaka', 'nishanthi@slsi.lk', '0715853402', '0715853402', '                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      ', NULL, '', '', '', '', 0, 150, '2024-09-05 15:05:25', 1, '2024-09-09 11:34:21', NULL, NULL, NULL);
