(387, 'Pharmaceutical Samples, Biological Samples', '1. Pharmaceutical Samples Active Pharmaceutical Ingredients (APIs): Used for purity testing, impurity profiling, and degradation product identification. Formulated Drugs: To assess the stability, quality control, and release profiles in pharmaceutical development. Pharmacokinetics/Pharmacodynamics Studies: Analysis of drugs and metabolites in biological matrices.  2. Biological Samples Blood (Plasma/Serum): For drug concentration measurement, metabolomics, and clinical diagnostics. Urine: Frequently used for drug testing, toxicology studies, and metabolic profiling. Tissue (Biopsy or Animal Tissues): For studying drug distribution, tissue-specific metabolism, or lipid profiling. 3. Food and Beverages For detecting pesticide residues, veterinary drug residues, and food additives. Used to analyze preservatives, contaminants, and natural compounds. 4. Environmental Samples Water (Surface, Groundwater, and Wastewater): Analyzed for pollutants, pharmaceutical residues, and organic contamina', '', 'Food and Beverages, Environmental Samples, Forensic Samples, Cosmetics and Personal Care Products,. Industrial Samples', '                  LCMS/MS 8030                                                                  ', 0, 572, NULL, '2024-09-25 14:21:00', NULL, 4, 0, 0, NULL),
